      "matchText": "Lucanas",
      "term": "Lucanas",
      "definition": "A small highland ethnic group of the south-central Andes, around the modern Ayacucho region of Peru, who lived as one of the dozens of minor polities surrounding Cuzco before being absorbed into the Inca state."
    },
    {
      "matchText": "Soras",
      "term": "Soras",
      "definition": "A small Quechua-speaking highland people of the south-central Peruvian Andes, neighbors of the Lucanas, who formed part of the patchwork of minor polities in the Cuzco region before Inca expansion swallowed them."
    },
    {
      "matchText": "Inca Urco",
      "term": "Inca Urco",
      "definition": "The designated heir of Viracocha Inca, remembered in the chronicles for his indolence. He fled Cuzco when the Chanka invaded; his half-brother Cusi Yupanqui (the future Pachacuti) defended the city instead and seized the throne, leaving Inca Urco disinherited."
    }
  ],
