      "matchText": "Tumbes",
      "term": "Tumbes",
      "definition": "A town and region on the far north coast of Peru, near the modern Ecuador border. In Inca times it marked the northern terminus of the coastal road and was one of the first Inca settlements the Spanish encountered when Pizarro's expedition reached the coast in the early 1530s."
    },
    {
      "matchText": "kamayoq",
      "term": "kamayoq",
      "definition": "A Quechua term meaning \"specialist\" or \"one charged with a task.\" In the Inca system the kamayoq were the resident staff who ran state installations such as the roadside tambos, maintaining buildings, preparing food and supplies for travelers, and reporting traffic to the regional governor."
    }
